From 69489af939568dfabda14b6b1dafbb139c6aa8b2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: arealjim <6187715+arealjim@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 16:53:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 05/23] runtime: refuse a second WiFi client while one is
 connected

The control thread accepted any ClientConnect while WiFi was enabled, whatever
the server state, and HandleClientConnect reset the tracking history and rebuilt
the encoder for the newcomer. A second client that connected while a headset was
streaming therefore took the session over, and two tracking clocks interleaved in
the single TrackingReceiver made the rendered head pose jump (violent shaking in
a Steam Frame when the desktop simulator auto-connected beside it, 2026-10-17).

A ClientConnect from a different address while a client is connected is now
refused, logged at most once per 5 s per address. The connected address may
always reconnect: that is how a lost ClientConnect is resent and how a restarted
client (new port, same host) gets back in before the liveness watchdog has
noticed. The port is deliberately not part of the identity.

The decision is a pure function in ClientAdmission.h with Catch2 tests, in the
style of ClientLiveness.h.

